{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>If you take a pledge.</b> After he said שלמת רעך, which is feminine, and likewise after כי היא כסותה לבדה, he said תשיבנו — the reference is to the pledge (חבול), which is masculine. The Gaon [Saadia] said: What is the reason for taking the pledge by day and returning it at night? He answered: because he fears lest he borrow from another and give it to him as a pledge in its place."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:37:25.985293746Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}